# How to Delete a GCP Project

## Key Points

- Shutting down a project stops all billing and resource usage. This action immediately moves the project into a 30-day recovery period.

- Project IDs are unique and permanent. Once a project is fully deleted, its ID can't be reused. If you want to preserve a custom project ID for future use, delete the resources within the project instead of shutting down the project itself.

- Resource recovery: While most resources are recoverable within the 30-day window, some services—such as Cloud Storage and Pub/Sub—might delete resources much sooner.

## Verify Project Status

```bash
gcloud projects describe PROJECT_ID